meta {
  name: lint expectations for ones that can never match or will not match as written
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/mockserver/lint
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  [
    {
      "httpRequest": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/users/.*"
      },
      "httpResponse": {
        "statusCode": 200
      }
    },
    {
      "httpRequest": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/users/1"
      },
      "httpResponse": {
        "statusCode": 404
      }
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Checks expectations for mistakes that stop them matching: a shadowed expectation (one evaluated earlier always matches first and never runs out), times or a time to live that allow no match, a percentage of 0, sequential responses that times never reaches, a path without a leading slash, with a scheme and host, with a query string, with a glob * or with a {name} template but no pathParameters, a misspelt method or header name, and (information only) STRICT JSON matching of a body with arrays. With expectations in the body (one or an array) it lints those without storing them; OpenAPI entries are skipped and invalid entries are reported as INVALID_EXPECTATION. With an empty body it lints the active stored expectations in the order they are evaluated. Advisory only: nothing is rejected or changed. The shadowing check compares at most 100,000 pairs and stops a regular expression that backtracks too long; shadowCheckTruncated says when either limit was reached.
  
  optional; expectations to lint without storing them. When empty, the active stored expectations are linted
  
  Full API reference: https://www.mock-server.com/mock_server/mockserver_clients.html
}
